 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per vertex. The calculation involves a fixed number of array lookups and a single arithmetic mean [S1, S2, unofficial]. The global pass is $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of voxels, as it processes each voxel and its 6 faces once [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ additional memory per vertex for the calculation. The lookup table `NEIGHBOR_VERTEX_LOOKUP` is a small static constant ($6 \times 4 \times 4$ integers), requiring negligible memory [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per vertex [G]. The calculation involves a fixed number of array lookups and a single arithmetic mean. The global pass is $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of voxels, as it processes each voxel and its 6 faces once [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ additional memory per vertex for the calculation [G]. The lookup table `NEIGHBOR_VERTEX_LOOKUP` is a small static constant ($6 \times 4 \times 4$ integers), requiring negligible memory [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Measured Performance:** The method is described as "cheap to calculate" because it only needs to be computed when the mesh is created, not per-frame [S2, unofficial]. It avoids the high cost of ray casting associated with standard ambient occlusion [S2, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths:** Produces smooth lighting transitions and naturally darkens concave areas (fake ambient occlusion) without complex shaders or ray tracing [S2, unofficial]. It is aesthetically pleasing for voxel worlds [S2, unofficial].
